            <ArticleTitle>Cyclosporine and graft coronary artery disease after heart transplantation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>121-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Risk factors for graft coronary artery disease after heart transplant are discussed in relationship to cyclosporine dosages. Patients receiving a mean cyclosporine dose higher than 4 mg/kg/day had lower incidence of graft coronary disease than patients receiving lower dosages.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
